+# DuskLight → RomRunner embedding notes
+
+RomRunner (`/Users/ry/Desktop/claude/GameShelf`) embeds this checkout's `platforms/android` module
+as a library, via `settings.gradle.kts`'s `includeBuild("../dusklight-src/platforms/android")`.
+
+## License / policy gate
+
+CC0-1.0 (public domain, see `LICENSE.md`). The README's "we do not accept contributions that are
+primarily AI-generated" clause governs pull requests back to this upstream repo — it does not
+restrict downstream reuse of CC0-licensed code in a separate project. No blocker, same conclusion
+reached for every other embedded core in RomRunner.
+
+## Local patches applied (none of these are upstreamed — this is a local, patched checkout only)
+
+1. **`platforms/android/app/build.gradle`**: `com.android.application` → `com.android.library`,
+   added `group = 'dev.twilitrealm'` / `version = 'embedded'` so RomRunner's composite build can
+   substitute `dev.twilitrealm:app` for this project.
+2. **`extern/borealis/platforms/android/gradle/borealis-application.gradle`**:
+   - Removed `applicationId`/`versionCode`/`versionName` from `defaultConfig` (invalid for a
+     library module — RomRunner, the consuming app, owns those now).
+   - Removed the `jniLibs.srcDirs = [stagedJniLibsDir]` line entirely. This module's native output
+     is hardcoded to `libmain.so` (see `extern/borealis/cmake/BorealisAndroid.cmake`'s
+     `set_target_properties(target PROPERTIES OUTPUT_NAME main)`), which is the EXACT same
+     filename PrimeHack's own Dolphin-core library uses, also embedded in RomRunner. Leaving both
+     wired into the standard jniLibs merge would let one silently win and the other's
+     `System.loadLibrary("main")` call resolve to completely wrong native code. Instead,
+     `libmain.so` is bundled as a plain RomRunner asset and side-loaded explicitly — see below.
+3. **`extern/borealis/platforms/android/java/dev/encounter/borealis/BorealisDocumentsProvider.java`**
+   (`authority()` method) + **`platforms/android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml`**: changed the
+   `BorealisDocumentsProvider`'s authority from `<packageName>.documents` to
+   `<packageName>.dusklight.documents` — RetroArch's own `RetroDocumentsProvider`, already embedded
+   in RomRunner, declares the identical `${applicationId}.documents` authority, which would
+   otherwise collide once merged.
+4. **`platforms/android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml`**: removed `DuskActivity`'s `LAUNCHER`
+   intent-filter category — RomRunner's own `MainActivity` is the sole launcher entry, matching
+   every other embedded core.
+5. **`platforms/android/app/src/main/java/com/twilitrealm/dusk/DuskActivity.java`**: three changes,
+   all needed together:
+   - An explicit `System.load(new File(getApplicationInfo().dataDir, "dusklight/libmain.so")...)`
+     call at the top of `onCreate()` — replacing the standard Borealis/SDL
+     `getLibraries() → System.loadLibrary("main")` mechanism, which searches `nativeLibraryDir`
+     (where `libmain.so` is deliberately absent per patch #2 above). RomRunner's
+     `DuskLightEmbeddedLauncher.ensureNativeLibInstalled()` extracts the bundled asset to this
+     exact path *before* starting the Activity, so the file already exists by the time this runs.
+   - Overrode `getLibraries()` to return `new String[0]`, so `SDLActivity.loadLibraries()` (called
+     from further up the `onCreate()` chain) doesn't *also* try `System.loadLibrary("main")` — a
+     second, bare-name load that would resolve against `nativeLibraryDir` and find PrimeHack's
+     copy instead. Safe to skip entirely: `BUILD_SHARED_LIBS=OFF` means SDL3 itself is statically
+     linked into this one `libmain.so`, so there's no separate `libSDL3.so` to load either.
+   - Overrode `getMainSharedObject()` to return the same explicit dataDir path. This was the
+     trickiest of the three to find: `SDLActivity.main()` doesn't use whatever was already
+     `System.load()`ed — it independently calls `getMainSharedObject()`
+     (default: `getApplicationInfo().nativeLibraryDir + "/libmain.so"`) and passes that path to a
+     *fresh* `dlopen()` in native code (`nativeRunMain` in `SDL_android.c`) purely to `dlsym()` the
+     `SDL_main` entry point. Left at its default, this silently `dlopen()`s PrimeHack's
+     `nativeLibraryDir` copy instead (same SONAME, different — wrong — code), producing "Couldn't
+     find function SDL_main in library .../lib/arm64/libmain.so" and a near-instant, exception-free
+     return from `main()` (looks like a clean quit, not a crash, from the Kotlin/Activity-lifecycle
+     side — this is the "why did it come back to the games list so fast" failure mode). Confirmed
+     `getMainSharedObject()` is designed to be overridden — that's what its doc comment says.
+6. **`extern/borealis/platforms/android/gradle/borealis-application.gradle`**: added
+   `consumerProguardFiles(project.file(androidConfig.proguardRules ?: 'proguard-rules.pro'))` to
+   `defaultConfig`. This is the mechanism (not `buildTypes.release.proguardFiles`, which only
+   affects a standalone build of this module) that actually propagates `-keep` rules into
+   RomRunner's own R8 pass — same lesson the RetroArch integration already learned. Matters here
+   because `androidConfig.proguardRules` in `app/build.gradle` resolves to **this module's own**
+   `platforms/android/app/proguard-rules.pro` (see #7) — not Borealis's own copy at
+   `extern/borealis/platforms/android/proguard-rules.pro`, which is a different file used only for
+   #6's `buildTypes.release.proguardFiles`.
+7. **`platforms/android/app/proguard-rules.pro`**: added `-keep class dev.twilitrealm.dusksdl.** { *; }`
+   (plus the Aurora/Borealis package equivalents, mirroring Borealis's own copy). Without this, R8
+   obfuscates/strips native-only JNI entry points like `SDLActivity.onNativeSoftReturnKey()` and
+   `SDLControllerManager.onNativeJoySensor(...)` as "unused" — nothing in *Java* calls them, only
+   `RegisterNatives` from native code does, which R8 has no visibility into. Symptom:
+   `NoSuchMethodError`/`Failed to register native method ... in ... classes2.dex` at runtime, even
+   though the method is genuinely declared in the source.
+8. **SDL3 Java package rename** (`org.libsdl.app` → `dev.twilitrealm.dusksdl`): ARMSX2 (also
+   embedded in RomRunner) vendors a *different* SDL3 point release (3.5.0 vs. this pin's 3.4.10)
+   under the identical Java package — a genuine API difference exists between them
+   (`SDLControllerManager.onNativePadDown`/`onNativePadUp` gained a parameter), so simply excluding
+   one copy at the Android build's duplicate-class step would silently break controller input in
+   whichever core lost. Renamed via a new CMake patch,
+   `extern/aurora/cmake/patches/apply-sdl3-java-package-rename.cmake`, wired into the `FetchContent`
+   step in `extern/aurora/cmake/AuroraSDL3Provider.cmake` (alongside the two patches already there)
+   — **this one persists automatically across re-fetches**, unlike patches #1–#7 above, which are
+   direct edits to tracked files and must be manually reapplied after a `git pull`/re-clone. The
+   patch renames the Java package/directory, the JNI export prefix (`SDL_JAVA_PREFIX` in
+   `SDL_android.c` and `hidapi/android/hid.cpp`), and the hardcoded `RegisterNatives` class-path
+   string literals (also in `SDL_android.c`) together, since none of these are derived from a
+   single shared constant. Three *tracked* (non-fetched) files also needed matching import/check
+   updates: `extern/aurora/cmake/AuroraSDL3Provider.cmake` and
+   `extern/borealis/cmake/BorealisAndroid.cmake` (both had a hardcoded
+   `IS_DIRECTORY ".../org/libsdl/app"` existence check), `extern/borealis/platforms/android/java/
+   dev/encounter/borealis/BorealisActivity.java` (`import org.libsdl.app.SDLActivity/SDLSurface`),
+   `extern/aurora/platforms/android/java/dev/encounter/aurora/AuroraSurface.java` (same), and
+   `extern/borealis/platforms/android/proguard-rules.pro` (the `-keep` rule itself, see #7).
+
+No custom `Application` subclass is declared anywhere in this module's manifest, so — unlike
+PrimeHack (`DolphinApplication`) and Cemu (`CemuApplication`) — no `initializeForEmbedding()` shim
+was needed in `RomRunnerApp.kt`.
+
+## Confirmed ROM launch argument
+
+`src/m_Do/m_Do_main.cpp`'s `game_main()` parses CLI args via `cxxopts`: the game file is `--dvd
+<path>` (also accepted positionally). `--backend <auto|d3d12|d3d11|metal|vulkan|null>` selects the
+graphics backend. `DuskActivity.getArguments()` reads these from the `dusk_argv` (String array) or
+`dusk_args` (single string) Intent extras — see `DuskLightEmbeddedLauncher.kt`.
+
+The engine opens the DVD path via plain SDL/C++ file I/O (no `content://` URI support for reads —
+confirmed via `extern/borealis/src/io.cpp`, which only special-cases `content://` for *write* mode).
+`DuskLightEmbeddedLauncher` resolves a real filesystem path via `SafPathUtils.realPathFromDocumentUri`
+before launching — same constraint, and same fallback (a Toast telling the user their ROMs folder
+needs to be on internal storage) `AzaharEmbeddedLauncher` already has for the same reason.
+
+## Rebuilding / updating this checkout later
+
+1. `git -C /Users/ry/Desktop/claude/dusklight-src pull` (or re-clone) — **patches #1–#7 above will
+   need to be re-applied** (direct edits to tracked files, not upstreamed). Patch #8 (the SDL3 Java
+   package rename) re-applies itself automatically on the next `cmake --preset` — it's a
+   `PATCH_COMMAND` hook, not a tracked-file edit. Diff against this file's description, or keep a
+   local patch/diff file if #1–#7 need to happen often.
+2. Rebuild the native library:
+   ```
+   export ANDROID_HOME=/Users/ry/Library/Android/sdk
+   export ANDROID_NDK_VERSION=29.0.14206865
+   export PATH="$ANDROID_HOME/cmake/3.31.6/bin:$PATH"
+   cd /Users/ry/Desktop/claude/dusklight-src
+   cmake --preset android-arm64
+   cmake --build --preset android-arm64
+   ```
+3. Strip debug symbols (the raw build output is ~340MB; stripped is ~45MB) and copy into
+   RomRunner's assets, replacing the existing copies:
+   ```
+   NDK=/Users/ry/Library/Android/sdk/ndk/29.0.14206865
+   "$NDK/toolchains/llvm/prebuilt/darwin-x86_64/bin/llvm-strip" --strip-debug --strip-unneeded \
+     build/android-arm64/libmain.so -o /tmp/libmain_stripped.so
+   cp /tmp/libmain_stripped.so ../GameShelf/app/src/main/assets/dusklight/libmain.so
+   rsync -a --delete res/ ../GameShelf/app/src/main/assets/res/
+   ```
+4. `cd ../GameShelf && ./gradlew :app:assembleDebug` (same composite-build wiring as every other
+   embedded core — no other steps needed unless DuskLight's own Gradle/manifest structure changed
+   upstream, in which case re-check patches #1–#5 above still apply cleanly).
diff --git a/platforms/android/app/build.gradle b/platforms/android/app/build.gradle
index aba966b448..3ce2eb43a6 100644
--- a/platforms/android/app/build.gradle
+++ b/platforms/android/app/build.gradle
@@ -1,5 +1,19 @@
 plugins {
-    id 'com.android.application'
+    id 'com.android.library'
+}
+
+// RomRunner integration: consumed as a library module via composite build (see
+// GameShelf/settings.gradle.kts / GAMESHELF_INTEGRATION.md), mirroring the same convention
+// already used for azahar-src/armsx2-src/primehack-src/cemu-src.
+group = 'dev.twilitrealm'
+version = 'embedded'
+
+// RomRunner integration: declared explicitly rather than relying on borealis-application.gradle's
+// own `compileSdk = androidConfig.compileSdk ?: 37` fallback below — AGP validates that a library
+// module's compileSdk is set before that shared script's `android {}` block ever runs, so the
+// fallback alone isn't sufficient here.
+android {
+    compileSdk = 37
 }
 
 def duskRepoDir = rootProject.projectDir.parentFile.parentFile
diff --git a/platforms/android/app/proguard-rules.pro b/platforms/android/app/proguard-rules.pro
index 308a46ab83..898397f80f 100644
--- a/platforms/android/app/proguard-rules.pro
+++ b/platforms/android/app/proguard-rules.pro
@@ -1 +1,11 @@
 -keep class dev.twilitrealm.dusk.DuskActivity { *; }
+# RomRunner integration: this is the file actually wired as consumerProguardFiles (see
+# borealis-application.gradle's defaultConfig) — Borealis's OWN copy of proguard-rules.pro (used
+# only for this module's own standalone release build, not propagated to a consuming app) has the
+# equivalent SDL/Aurora/Borealis JNI keep rules, but they need to ALSO live here to actually reach
+# RomRunner's own R8 pass. Without this, R8 strips/renames native-only JNI entry points like
+# SDLControllerManager.onNativeJoySensor() as "unused"/obfuscatable, since RegisterNatives calls
+# from native code aren't a call site R8 can see.
+-keep class dev.twilitrealm.dusksdl.** { *; }
+-keep class dev.encounter.aurora.** { *; }
+-keep class dev.encounter.borealis.** { *; }
